%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Casey_Victim
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Casey
  isScammer: 0
  steps:
  - npcLine: Ethan? It's Casey. I'm a lawyer for your grandson. He's in jail after
      an accident.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Ethan, wait. We don''t know a Casey. This sounds like a
      ''Grandparent Scam.'''
    choices:
    - text: Oh my god! Is he okay? What do I need to do?
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: Which grandson are you talking about? Give me a name.
      type: good
      pointValue: 12
    - text: Let me call his parents and see what's going on.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: He's terrified and doesn't want his parents to know. He'll be furious
      if you call them.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Secrecy is a huge red flag. They want to isolate you so
      you don''t check the facts.'
    choices:
    - text: Okay, I won't tell them. How much is the bail?
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: If it's an emergency, his parents need to know. I'm calling them.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Why can't he call me himself?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: The judge set bail at $4,000. We need it in gift cards immediately to
      process it today.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: $4,000 in gift cards? No legitimate court or lawyer accepts
      payment like that.'
    choices:
    - text: I'll head to the store now. Tell him I'm coming.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Lawyers take wire transfers or checks, not gift cards. This is a scam.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can I pay with a credit card over the phone instead?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Every minute you wait, he stays in a holding cell with dangerous criminals.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: He''s using fear and urgency to stop you from thinking
      clearly.'
    choices:
    - text: I'm so worried... okay, I'm at the store. What cards do I buy?
      type: bad
      pointValue: -14
    - text: If he's really in jail, I'll visit the precinct in person.
      type: good
      pointValue: 13
    - text: Can you send me a picture of him to prove he's there?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: There's no time for visits! The courier is waiting for the codes now.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: He''s pushing harder because you''re asking questions.
      Stay firm.'
    choices:
    - text: Fine! The code is 4920-3841-...
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Hanging up now. I'm calling the actual police station to verify.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Wait, I need to make sure I have enough in my account.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: If you hang up, the deal is off and he'll be transferred to state prison.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: That''s not how the legal system works. He''s lying to
      scare you.'
    choices:
    - text: Please don't let that happen! I'll give you the rest of the money.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: State prison? For a car accident bail hearing? You're a fraud.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can I talk to my grandson for one second?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: He's in processing. He can't talk. Just give me the codes and he's free.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Notice how he has an excuse for everything? Don''t fall
      for it.'
    choices:
    - text: Okay, I'm reading the numbers now...
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Real lawyers don't act like high-pressure salesmen. Goodbye.
      type: good
      pointValue: 14
    - text: Which store should I go to for the best cards?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Go to the nearest pharmacy. Hurry, Ethan. His future is in your hands.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Using guilt is a low blow. You''re doing the right thing
      by refusing.'
    choices:
    - text: I'm going. I can't let him stay in there.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: My grandson's future is safe because I'm not giving you a cent.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can I pay half now and half later?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: No! It has to be the full amount. Do you want to save him or not?
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Last chance, Ethan. Hang up and call the family.'
    choices:
    - text: I'll do it. Just please help him.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I'm calling my grandson's cell phone right now. Goodbye.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Why are you being so mean about this?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  successEnding: You avoided the emotional trap! Urgency, secrecy, and requests for
    gift cards are hallmark signs of vishing.
  failureEnding: 'You fell for the emotional manipulation. Scammers use fear for
    loved ones and secrecy to isolate their victims[cite: 1].'
